{
  "_id": "tg-bless-verb",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "God blessed them, saying, Be fruitful, Gen. 1:22 (Moses 2:22). blessed the seventh day, Gen. 2:3 (Ex. 20:11; Moses 3:3). God blessed Noah and his sons, Gen. 9:1. I will bless thee, and make thy name great, Gen. 12:2. in thee shall all … be blessed, Gen. 12:3 (18:18; Gal. 3:8). That in blessing I will bless thee, Gen. 22:17 (Heb. 6:14). in thy seed shall all the nations of the earth be blessed, Gen. 22:18 (26:4; 28:14; Acts 3:25). my soul may bless thee before I die, Gen. 27:4. he discerned him not … so he blessed him, Gen. 27:23. I will not let thee go, except thou bless me, Gen. 32:26. blessed the Egyptian’s house for Joseph’s sake, Gen. 39:5. Bring them … and I will bless them, Gen. 48:9. he blessed them … saying, In thee shall Israel bless, Gen. 48:20. Almighty, who shall bless thee with blessings, Gen. 49:25. I will come unto thee, and I will bless thee, Ex. 20:24. he shall bless thy bread, and thy water, Ex. 23:25. Lord bless thee, and keep thee, Num. 6:24. it pleased the Lord to bless Israel, Num. 24:1. will love thee, and bless thee, Deut. 7:13. Thou shalt be blessed above all people, Deut. 7:14. stand upon mount Gerizim to bless the people, Deut. 27:12. Moses the man of God blessed … Israel, Deut. 33:1. child grew, and the Lord blessed him, Judg. 13:24. Eli blessed Elkanah and his wife, 1 Sam. 2:20. Levites arose and blessed the people, 2 Chr. 30:27. Ezra blessed the Lord, Neh. 8:6. Lord blessed the latter end of Job more, Job 42:12. thou, Lord, wilt bless the righteous, Ps. 5:12. bless with their mouth, but they curse inwardly, Ps. 62:4. bless our God, ye people, Ps. 66:8. He will bless them that fear the Lord, Ps. 115:13. Lord shall bless thee out of Zion, Ps. 128:5. He that hath a bountiful eye shall be blessed, Prov. 22:9. I called him alone, and blessed him, Isa. 51:2 (2 Ne. 8:2). they are the seed which the Lord hath blessed, Isa. 61:9. nations shall bless themselves in him, Jer. 4:2. from this day will I bless you, Hag. 2:19.",
